<resources>
    <!--
      Burmese (my-MM).

      Every key in the default `values/strings.xml` is translated here, including the emoji
      scales and the "%1$s %2$s" pass-throughs, which are identical by definition. A missing
      key would silently fall back to English, so `BurmeseStringsTest` compares the two files
      key for key and also checks that the format specifiers match.

      Digits stay Latin. Burmese conventionally writes Myanmar digits, but every count in this
      app reaches the string through `%1$d`, which formats with the platform's default
      numbering. Rendering Myanmar digits would mean converting numbers before substitution
      across the whole app; the mixing that causes is why this is deliberately uniform for
      now rather than half-converted.
    -->

